--- SURFACE IMPLEMENTATION (parity with web ChartsRow.tsx) ---
Web source: web/src/features/charging/components/charging-list/ChartsRow.tsx (presentational; sole hook
useTranslation; props energyTrend / chargerBreakdown / costByType). Native follows the ChargingBreakdownSlide
precedent for a pure presentational web component: a model-driven view + WinUI-free projection, no Source/
ViewModel (the owning charging-list page owns the query lifecycle; error/stale/offline are handled once before
this row is composed — documented in ChartsRow.Model.cs).

Files (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/):
  ChartsRow.Model.cs - input records (EnergyTrendPoint / ChargerBreakdownEntry / CostByTypeEntry mirroring
                       helpers.ts), ChartsRowProjection (loading -> empty -> ready; per-panel HasData; donut
                       palette-by-order; 2-decimal value formatting = web _globalPrecision), display records,
                       view.opened diagnostics (slug=ChartsRow), registration.
  ChartsRow.cs       - WinUI view (ContentControl). Responsive 2-col grid (web grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2),
                       each panel a TsGlassPanel entering via TsFadeIn (delays 100/150ms). Panel 1: Calendar-
                       accented header + TsComposedChart (energy Area[Role=Energy] + cost Line) + date-range
                       caption. Panel 2: Plug-accented header + TsPieChart(donut) + per-type energy/cost/$-per-kWh
                       rows. Every panel shows a friendly TsEmptyState when its half has no data (never a blank
                       box); loading shows skeleton chrome. Narrator names on surface/panels/charts/cost rows;
                       reduce-motion honoured by TsFadeIn.
Tests: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/ChartsRowTests.cs (41 tests: state precedence, per-panel
  gating, trend point mapping, date range, donut palette-by-order, grouped/2-decimal formatting, localized
  series names + cost strings, i18n key resolution (KeyEcho), a11y names, PII-safe diagnostics, arg validation).
  Linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (ChartsRow.Model.cs) so the projection is verified headlessly.

i18n (ADR-016): all keys already present in apps/shared/i18n/catalog (en/ar/he) — NO catalog edits:
